        "username": "rjc917",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rjc917/{size}/1888_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-29T02:47:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I play Sentinels at least once a week on the videogame, but for Tabletop Day, I wanted to get out the old cards.&nbsp; I was playing with my mom, who hadn't played in a while, and I had just listened to the GtG origin story extrasode where Christopher said everyone's first game should be against Baron Blade.&nbsp; So even though it wasn't quite her first time, I decided we should fight the Baron.&nbsp; Should make for a fun, simple game, right?</p><p>My mom decided to play as Ra, because she sort of remembered using him before and chose Atlantis as the environment.&nbsp; I played as Mister Fixer and the Scholar, because she wanted to see how the Scholar worked.&nbsp; Normally I don't think Atlantis is as difficult an environment as people say, but today it was pretty rough on us.&nbsp; But the real killer was Blade's two Living Force Fields and a Backlash Field and realizing we had picked a team with no ongoing destruction between them.&nbsp; We managed to get Blade down to 1hp on his front side before we lost.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:13.277Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
