        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/{size}/4833_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-29T15:35:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"The Girl With No Name\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n The Girl With No Name:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Honestly, the reason I didn't believe the Wardens operated out of Atlantis is because, well… I can barely survive a game there, and you're telling me they live there?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think about it in kind of a “we operate out of these buildings and can use rooms x, y, and z elsewhere” for them using it as a base. Villain fights are wide-ranging affairs that include less predictable parts of the place; either because the villains are trying to use those more exotic power sources or just because it’s a running battle all over the place.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
